Theorem L-2: Product lattice + AimsState + AimsStateMap + sentinels

  Preconditions:
    - The 7 per-dimension lattices are authored at
      aims-proof/proofs/01-lattice/Lattice.proof (theorem L-1)
    - Product lattice = componentwise join over the 7 dimensions
      + canonicalization per Annex E §AIMS
    - AimsState = the 7-tuple state value per the canonical proof notation
      sec-AimsState-Representation
    - AimsStateMap = per-block / per-instruction map carrying AimsState values
      per Annex E §AIMS §7 AimsStateMap row
    - Sentinels SCALAR, FRESH, CONSERVATIVE, ALL, NONE are special-cased
      per Annex E §AIMS + Appendix A + L-9

  Soundness property:
    AimsState definition (7-tuple in canonical dimension order; per
    the canonical proof notation:42):

      AimsState = <Access, Consumption, Cardinality, Uniqueness, Locality, Shape, Effect>

      Canonical authored form for a single state (parenthesized, comma-separated):
        (O, L, 1, u, bl, R_S, {alloc})

    AimsStateMap definition (per Annex E §AIMS §7 AimsStateMap row +
    Annex E §AIMS IA backward dataflow):

      AimsStateMap = CfgNode -> AimsState

      Concretely the per-function backward-dataflow result carrying:
        - block_entry_states: BlockIndex -> Map ArcVarId AimsState
        - block_exit_states: BlockIndex -> Map ArcVarId AimsState
        - converged value: Map ArcVarId AimsState at function exit

      Position-keyed entries (entry_states, exit_states, instr_states) are
      invalidated by merge_blocks() per Annex E §AIMS §6 PL-3 invariant;
      step 10 realize_annotations() consults AimsStateMap via ArcVarId-keyed
      lookups exclusively.

    Sentinel definitions (per the canonical proof notation sec-AimsState-Representation
    lines 54-58):

      SCALAR:
        per-dimension sentinel; NOT a lattice element per L-9
        analysis SHALL exclude SCALAR-marked variables from the state map
        join with SCALAR is undefined; canonicalize MUST NOT propagate SCALAR
        emitted by TF-1, TF-2a, TF-10, TF-10a per Appendix A

      FRESH(shape):
        canonical TF-3 output for newly-allocated values
        FRESH(shape) = (O, L, 1, u, bl, shape, {alloc})
        all 7 dimensions instantiated; Effect set carries may_alloc only
        Uniqueness = u is load-bearing for DP-6 reuse eligibility

      CONSERVATIVE:
        canonical TF-5 default for unknown calls / indirect dispatch
        CONSERVATIVE = (O, U, omega, ms, top, Phi, ALL)
        Uniqueness = ms (NOT s) enables dynamic COW per DP-4
        NOT lattice TOP; operationally correct default

      ALL:
        Effect flag set = {may_alloc, may_share, may_throw}
        unknown-call effect default per TF-5 / TF-5a / TF-6b / TF-6c

      NONE:
        Effect flag set = {} (empty)
        TF-4 Project + TF-10 IsShared + TF-10a Reset default

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-02 lattice algebra proofs (product correctness)

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (product-join componentwise definition + canonicalization)
      monotonicity (validates product join preserves L-6 from per-dim joins)

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-02 discharges product lattice + sentinel theorems
